<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Army Personnel Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Army Personnel Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Army Personnel Recovery involves military efforts taken to prepare for and execute the recovery and reintegration of isolated personnel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isolated Personnel">
  <data key="d0">Isolated Personnel</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Personnel who are separated from their unit due to enemy action, disorientation, or environmental conditions and require recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Isolated Personnel are individuals separated from their unit or friendly control due to enemy action, disorientation, or environmental conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516fa4bb2c82a8017519f0c1ee450177</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commander">
  <data key="d0">Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who defines operational areas, assigns areas of operations to subordinates, and manages terrain and fires.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual responsible for conducting operations, clearing fires, and ensuring security within an assigned area.&lt;SEP&gt;A commander is an individual responsible for synchronizing combat power, defining areas of operations, and managing areas of influence.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commander is the individual assigned an Area of Operations (AO) responsible for recovering and returning isolated persons to friendly control.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual responsible for employing forces, designating engagement areas, and directing operations to achieve positional advantages.&lt;SEP&gt;A leader who assumes risk, task-organizes capabilities, and weights the decisive operation to accomplish the mission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8cfc7a602ac472213d15ef41cf6d81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-272b00f6d97de5a3de8f78e2d6a7851e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516fa4bb2c82a8017519f0c1ee450177</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Area of Operations">
  <data key="d0">Area of Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">An operational area defined by a commander for land and maritime forces that is large enough to accomplish missions and protect forces.&lt;SEP&gt;An area of operations is an operational area defined by a commander for land and maritime forces that should be large enough to accomplish missions and protect forces.&lt;SEP&gt;An Area of Operations is a geographical area assigned to a commander who holds responsibility for recovering isolated persons within its bounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-272b00f6d97de5a3de8f78e2d6a7851e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immediate Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Immediate Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Immediate Recovery is a response triggered without detailed planning in the event of isolation, requiring analysis of mission variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deliberate Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Deliberate Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deliberate Recovery is a planned operation conducted when immediate recovery is not undertaken or is unsuccessful.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airspace Control">
  <data key="d0">Airspace Control</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Airspace Control consists of capabilities and procedures used to increase operational effectiveness by promoting the safe, efficient, and flexible use of airspace.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Division Joint Air-Ground Integration Center">
  <data key="d0">Division Joint Air-Ground Integration Center</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Division Joint Air-Ground Integration Center (JAGIC) is an organization composed of the Army's fires cell, air missile defense cell, airspace element, and USAF's air support operations center and tactical air control party.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airspace Element">
  <data key="d0">Airspace Element</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Airspace Element is the functional lead for the division staff, responsible for integrating airspace operations and developing standard operating procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Support Operations Center">
  <data key="d0">Air Support Operations Center</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Air Support Operations Center (ASOC) is a United States Air Force unit co-located with the division headquarters to command and control air operations.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization that provides an effective means to coordinate suppression of enemy air defense in division-assigned airspace.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Air Control Party">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Air Control Party</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Tactical Air Control Party is a unit co-located with the division headquarters and part of the airspace control working group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airspace Control Authority">
  <data key="d0">Airspace Control Authority</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Airspace Control Authority is the entity responsible for assigning a volume of airspace to the division headquarters.&lt;SEP&gt;The authority responsible for delegating the control of airspace to a division in accordance with plans and orders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airspace Control Working Group">
  <data key="d0">Airspace Control Working Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Airspace Control Working Group integrates airspace operations with functional and integrating cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Theater Airspace Control Plan">
  <data key="d0">Theater Airspace Control Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Theater Airspace Control Plan is a document that the airspace element plans and updates with input to ensure consistency with joint procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United States Air Force">
  <data key="d0">United States Air Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States Air Force aligns air support operations center capabilities with Army divisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The military service branch that operates air support operations centers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FM 3-50">
  <data key="d0">FM 3-50</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">FM 3-50 is a field manual providing information on Army personnel recovery and the operations process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 3-52">
  <data key="d0">JP 3-52</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">JP 3-52 is a joint publication defining airspace control capabilities and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;A joint publication that provides the definition for coordinating altitude and coordination level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fires Cell">
  <data key="d0">Fires Cell</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Fires Cell is a component of the division joint air-ground integration center (JAGIC).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Missile Defense Cell">
  <data key="d0">Air Missile Defense Cell</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Air Missile Defense Cell is a component of the division joint air-ground integration center (JAGIC).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Task Force Components">
  <data key="d0">Joint Task Force Components</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint Task Force Components are supported by Army forces during external supported recovery operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interagency Organizations">
  <data key="d0">Interagency Organizations</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Interagency Organizations are supported by Army forces during external supported recovery operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multinational Forces">
  <data key="d0">Multinational Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Multinational Forces receive airspace control support from the division headquarters and are supported during recovery operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces with whom the special operations command–forward synchronizes efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Army Battlefield Coordination Detachment">
  <data key="d0">Army Battlefield Coordination Detachment</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Army Battlefield Coordination Detachment coordinates with the division airspace element through its airspace section.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brigade">
  <data key="d0">Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Brigade is a subordinate unit to which the division headquarters may delegate airspace management responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;An Army echelon higher than a battalion and part of a division.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit consisting of two or more battalions and a headquarters company or detachment, normally containing 2,500 to 5,000 Soldiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Close Air Support">
  <data key="d0">Close Air Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Close Air Support is an operation commanded and controlled by the Air Support Operations Center.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suppression of Enemy Air Defense">
  <data key="d0">Suppression of Enemy Air Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A military operation coordinated by air support operations centers within division-assigned airspace.&lt;SEP&gt;Suppression of Enemy Air Defense is an operation coordinated by the Air Support Operations Center within division-assigned airspace.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airspace Control Order">
  <data key="d0">Airspace Control Order</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An order implementing the airspace control plan.&lt;SEP&gt;An Airspace Control Order is a document into which airspace requirements are integrated.&lt;SEP&gt;A document into which special operations requests are coordinated by the special operations liaison element.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b01db05e3701dde254ad8d25610798</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ATP 3-92">
  <data key="d0">ATP 3-92</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">ATP 3-92 is a publication containing information on the airspace element's responsibilities when the division is an operational headquarters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ATP 3-91.1">
  <data key="d0">ATP 3-91.1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A publication containing descriptions of functions related to requesting authority to control division-assigned airspace.&lt;SEP&gt;ATP 3-91.1 describes functions regarding the request for authority to control division-assigned airspace.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meeting Engagement">
  <data key="d0">Meeting Engagement</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A combat action that occurs when a moving force, incompletely deployed for battle, engages an enemy at an unexpected time and place.&lt;SEP&gt;A combat action that occurs when a force makes unexpected contact with an enemy or when opponents are aware of each other and decide to attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8cfc7a602ac472213d15ef41cf6d81</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconnaissance">
  <data key="d0">Reconnaissance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The active collection of information, usually including human participation, that produces combat information.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission undertaken to obtain information, the ineffectiveness of which often leads to meeting engagements.&lt;SEP&gt;A method used to gather information; its ineffectiveness can lead to unexpected contact and meeting engagements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8cfc7a602ac472213d15ef41cf6d81</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initiative">
  <data key="d0">Initiative</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A strategic imperative in combat where a force acts first to gain an advantage, often seized through prompt execution of battle drills.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battle Drills">
  <data key="d0">Battle Drills</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rehearsed and well-understood actions made in response to common battlefield occurrences, requiring a "go" order instead of a plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Movement">
  <data key="d0">Movement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The positioning of combat power to establish conditions for maneuver, directed through techniques and formations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maneuver">
  <data key="d0">Maneuver</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The employment of forces through movement in combination with fires and information to achieve a position of advantage.&lt;SEP&gt;A tactical action enabled by movement, used to obtain positional advantage over an enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;A principle of war closely associated with the concept of weighting the decisive operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8cfc7a602ac472213d15ef41cf6d81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mutual Support">
  <data key="d0">Mutual Support</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Support that units render each other against an enemy based on assigned tasks, relative position, and inherent capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supporting Range">
  <data key="d0">Supporting Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The distance one unit can be separated from another while remaining within the maximum range of its weapons systems.&lt;SEP&gt;One of two aspects of mutual support, referring to the ability to support with direct or indirect fires.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supporting Distance">
  <data key="d0">Supporting Distance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The distance between two units that allows one to aid the other in time to prevent defeat or regain control.&lt;SEP&gt;One of two aspects of mutual support, equaling supporting range when friendly forces are static.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operation">
  <data key="d0">Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A sequence of tactical actions with a common purpose, including planning, preparing, executing, and assessing offensive, defensive, and stability tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Framework">
  <data key="d0">Operational Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A cognitive tool used to assist commanders in visualizing and describing the application of combat power in time, space, purpose, and resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AO (Area of Operations)">
  <data key="d0">AO (Area of Operations)</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">An area assigned to a commander for the conduct of operations, serving as a component of the operational framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Areas">
  <data key="d0">Deep Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Areas designated by commanders within their AO to describe the physical arrangement of forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Close Areas">
  <data key="d0">Close Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Areas designated by commanders within their AO as part of the operational framework's physical arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support Areas">
  <data key="d0">Support Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Areas designated by commanders within their AO to facilitate operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consolidation Areas">
  <data key="d0">Consolidation Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Areas designated by commanders within their AO to describe the physical arrangement of forces in time, space, and purpose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decisive Operations">
  <data key="d0">Decisive Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Operations established by commanders to articulate the purpose of an operation, directly leading to mission accomplishment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shaping Operations">
  <data key="d0">Shaping Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Shaping Operations are secondary efforts where minimum essential combat power is expended to support the decisive operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations where commanders expend minimum essential combat power to support the decisive operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations established by commanders to create conditions for decisive operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations conducted by a division headquarters to create favorable conditions for the success of subordinate units.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations conducted by a division headquarters within its area of operations to create favorable conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8cfc7a602ac472213d15ef41cf6d81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43827b67edd15288722ea2a5a3a94f03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sustaining Operations">
  <data key="d0">Sustaining Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Operations established by commanders to enable decisive and shaping operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Piecemeal Commitment">
  <data key="d0">Piecemeal Commitment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The immediate employment of units in combat as they become available, often unsynchronized, which risks defeat in detail.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defeat in Detail">
  <data key="d0">Defeat in Detail</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A technique of concentrating overwhelming combat power against separate parts of a force rather than defeating the entire force at once.&lt;SEP&gt;The destruction of smaller committed forces, a risk associated with piecemeal commitment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43827b67edd15288722ea2a5a3a94f03</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconstitution">
  <data key="d0">Reconstitution</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A total process performed by commanders to raise combat effectiveness, involving tasks like removing units from combat and reestablishing cohesion.&lt;SEP&gt;Actions planned and implemented by commanders to restore units to a desired level of combat effectiveness, including regeneration and reorganization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regeneration">
  <data key="d0">Regeneration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A process at the tactical level that requires support from higher echelons to restore units.&lt;SEP&gt;A component of reconstitution that requires support from higher echelons to restore a unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reorganization">
  <data key="d0">Reorganization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A component of reconstitution possible at the tactical level to restore a unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commanders">
  <data key="d0">Commanders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Leaders who perform enabling operations, consider mission variables, and use warfighting functions to accomplish missions.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals responsible for integrating environmental considerations, planning operations, requesting resources, and balancing stability tasks with combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals responsible for performing reconstitution, constituting reserves, and adhering to rules of engagement.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaders responsible for visualizing operations, assigning areas, and implementing reconstitution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dfd7a87dfd28f5856896abb13b5c87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43827b67edd15288722ea2a5a3a94f03</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Movement Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Movement Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Techniques used by Army forces to direct movement and mitigate the risk of unexpected enemy contact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Movement Formations">
  <data key="d0">Movement Formations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Formations used by Army forces to direct movement and establish conditions for maneuver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Fires">
  <data key="d0">Direct Fires</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire delivered directly at the enemy, utilized by units to support each other and prevent enemy engagement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indirect Fires">
  <data key="d0">Indirect Fires</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire delivered at a target not visible to the firer, utilized by units to provide mutual support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infiltration">
  <data key="d0">Infiltration</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of maneuver involving movement by small groups through enemy positions.&lt;SEP&gt;An enemy action characterized by covert movement into an area, which mutual support helps to prevent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Offense">
  <data key="d0">Offense</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the four elements of decisive action involving offensive operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of military operation where commanders maneuver subordinate forces to ensure mutual support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dfd7a87dfd28f5856896abb13b5c87</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defense">
  <data key="d0">Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the four elements of decisive action involving defensive operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of military operation where commanders select tactical positions to achieve maximum mutual support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dfd7a87dfd28f5856896abb13b5c87</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stability Operations">
  <data key="d0">Stability Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of operations included within the scope of an operation, focused on maintaining order.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enabling Operations">
  <data key="d0">Enabling Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Operations performed by commanders to help in the planning, preparation, and execution of decisive action elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations included in the sequence of tactical actions to support the achievement of objectives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dfd7a87dfd28f5856896abb13b5c87</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Main Effort">
  <data key="d0">Main Effort</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A focus of operations where the commander concentrates combat power to achieve results.&lt;SEP&gt;A designation by commanders to prioritize the shifting of resources within the operational framework.&lt;SEP&gt;A tactical concept that can be weighted by commanders, often closely associated with the decisive operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supporting Effort">
  <data key="d0">Supporting Effort</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A designation by commanders to support the prioritization of resources within the operational framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Momentum">
  <data key="d0">Momentum</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical quality that piecemeal commitment may be advantageous to maintain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mass">
  <data key="d0">Mass</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The concentration of combat power, which piecemeal commitment fails to ensure.&lt;SEP&gt;A principle of war closely associated with the concept of weighting the decisive operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfc767a21213904a266f2129f2b1351e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Division Headquarters">
  <data key="d0">Division Headquarters</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A division headquarters leverages joint force capabilities, conducts shaping operations, allocates resources, designates efforts, and establishes priorities for subordinate units.&lt;SEP&gt;A self-contained organization with a command group and a fully functional staff that BCTs synchronize plans and actions for to accomplish tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subordinate Units">
  <data key="d0">Subordinate Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Units that cooperate to accomplish a mission as directed by the concept of operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Military units that may become combat ineffective and require reconstitution.&lt;SEP&gt;Units that operate under a division headquarters, receiving resources and support priorities to achieve success.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43827b67edd15288722ea2a5a3a94f03</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corps">
  <data key="d0">Corps</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A higher echelon headquarters that can integrate functional brigade airspace requirements and task multifunctional support brigades.&lt;SEP&gt;The highest Army echelon mentioned, consisting of divisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A corps is an echelon of command and tactical formation that employs divisions and brigades to achieve objectives on land, exercising operational control over Army divisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A Corps receives complementary effects supporting freedom of action from special operations joint task forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Corps is a military unit level that requires a Psychological Operations group for command and control capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ba37bc0e16b243f02ab5b7be2e100c</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755291</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Divisions">
  <data key="d0">Divisions</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactical units employed by a corps to achieve objectives on land, typically numbering two to five under a corps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-functional Brigades">
  <data key="d0">Multi-functional Brigades</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Brigades employed by a corps or field army to achieve objectives on land.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of brigade employed by a division to achieve objectives on land.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Brigades">
  <data key="d0">Functional Brigades</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Brigades employed by a corps or field army to achieve objectives on land, providing specific functional support.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of brigade employed by a division to achieve objectives on land.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large-scale Combat Operations">
  <data key="d0">Large-scale Combat Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Large-scale combat operations are a type of military operation where units performing close combat are unlikely to conduct stability tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;High-intensity operations that require specific considerations for personnel recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations that may require a corps headquarters to function as a tactical land headquarters or the establishment of a field army.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-272b00f6d97de5a3de8f78e2d6a7851e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516fa4bb2c82a8017519f0c1ee450177</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Force Land Component Command">
  <data key="d0">Joint Force Land Component Command</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">An operational-level command role that a field army or corps may serve as, requiring augmentation from joint and multinational forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Theater Army">
  <data key="d0">Theater Army</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">An organization that provides capabilities and units to a corps for conducting operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The theater army provides resources to support and sustain Special Forces long-term operations in established combat theaters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marine Corps Units">
  <data key="d0">Marine Corps Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Units over which a corps exercises tactical control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multinational Units">
  <data key="d0">Multinational Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Units over which a corps exercises tactical control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field Army">
  <data key="d0">Field Army</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A field army is an echelon of command that employs multiple corps and brigades, serving as the senior tactical or operational-level command.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corps Commander">
  <data key="d0">Corps Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The individual responsible for determining appropriate command and support relationships for subordinate divisions and brigades within a corps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARFOR">
  <data key="d0">ARFOR</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Army Forces; a role served by the field army for multi-corps operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Army component and senior Army headquarters of all Army forces assigned or attached to a combatant command.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peer and Near-peer Adversaries">
  <data key="d0">Peer and Near-peer Adversaries</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversaries capable of conducting large-scale ground combat, influencing the deployment of field armies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Area of Responsibility">
  <data key="d0">Area of Responsibility</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The geographic area assigned to a field army, tailored by the Army to prevailing conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maneuver Enhancement Brigade">
  <data key="d0">Maneuver Enhancement Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of unit whose organizational design allows it to be assigned an area of operations, similar to a Brigade Combat Team.&lt;SEP&gt;A brigade capable of and responsible for airspace management of Army airspace users within their area of operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit generally required by a corps to conduct large-scale combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit assigned to a division conducting large-scale ground combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of multifunctional support brigade.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Aviation Brigade">
  <data key="d0">Combat Aviation Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A unit generally required by a corps to conduct large-scale combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit assigned to a division conducting large-scale ground combat operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of multifunctional support brigade.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expeditionary Sustainment Command">
  <data key="d0">Expeditionary Sustainment Command</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A unit generally required by a corps to conduct large-scale combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field Artillery Brigade">
  <data key="d0">Field Artillery Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A unit required by a corps for large-scale combat operations, generally not retained in reserve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AO">
  <data key="d0">AO</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Area of Operations where a division headquarters conducts shaping operations to create favorable conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Units">
  <data key="d0">Functional Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Units including military police, engineer, air and missile defense, and military intelligence that operate in command or support relationships with a division.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Combat Support Agencies">
  <data key="d0">Joint Combat Support Agencies</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Agencies that provide support to a corps alongside theater military intelligence and signal organizations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Theater Military Intelligence Brigade">
  <data key="d0">Theater Military Intelligence Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A brigade required by a corps to conduct large-scale combat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consolidation of Gains Activities">
  <data key="d0">Consolidation of Gains Activities</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Activities for which field artillery brigades are not used, unlike other brigades that may be retained for this purpose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="The Army">
  <data key="d0">The Army</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The overarching organization that tailors each field army to the conditions prevailing in its assigned area of responsibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f675a29b15c1691c9d14df4800ef9dcf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platoon">
  <data key="d0">Platoon</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A subdivision of a company consisting of two or more squads or sections, normally led by a lieutenant.&lt;SEP&gt;A subdivision of a company or troop consisting of two or more squads or sections, normally led by a lieutenant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Company">
  <data key="d0">Company</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit subdivided into platoons.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit consisting of two or more platoons, usually of the same type, with a headquarters and a limited capacity for self-support.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit that can be attached to or detached from Brigade Combat Teams or their organic battalions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Troop">
  <data key="d0">Troop</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of military unit equivalent to a company.&lt;SEP&gt;A company-size unit in a cavalry organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery">
  <data key="d0">Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of military unit equivalent to a company.&lt;SEP&gt;A company-size unit in a field artillery or air defense artillery battalion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Detachment">
  <data key="d0">Detachment</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical element organized on either a temporary or permanent basis for special duties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battalion">
  <data key="d0">Battalion</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">An Army echelon higher than a company and part of a brigade.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit consisting of two or more company-, battery-, or troop-size units and a headquarters, typically ranging from 500 to 800 Soldiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Squadron">
  <data key="d0">Squadron</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A unit echelon in cavalry organizations equivalent to a battalion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regiment">
  <data key="d0">Regiment</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A higher echelon unit than a battalion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Group">
  <data key="d0">Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A higher echelon unit than a battalion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brigade Combat Team">
  <data key="d0">Brigade Combat Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of maneuver unit to which commanders normally assign areas of operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A combined arms organization consisting of a brigade headquarters, at least two maneuver battalions, and necessary supporting functional capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;A combined arms organization consisting of a brigade headquarters, at least two maneuver battalions, and necessary supporting functional capabilities, serving as the largest fixed tactical units in the Army.&lt;SEP&gt;A military unit typically supported by a Civil Affairs company during deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;A Brigade Combat Team receives complementary effects supporting freedom of action from special operations joint task forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a07dcb1b08c46f988ffe232de0ba6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755291</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Company Team">
  <data key="d0">Company Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A combined arms organization formed by attaching one or more nonorganic platoons to a company.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Task Force">
  <data key="d0">Task Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A maneuver battalion-size unit formed by task-organizing subordinate maneuver battalions with support companies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lieutenant">
  <data key="d0">Lieutenant</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A rank that normally leads a platoon.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who normally leads a platoon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Squad">
  <data key="d0">Squad</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A small military unit typically containing two or more fire teams, usually led by a staff sergeant.&lt;SEP&gt;A subunit that forms part of a platoon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section">
  <data key="d0">Section</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical unit smaller than a platoon and larger than a squad, used by the Army and Marine Corps.&lt;SEP&gt;A subunit that forms part of a platoon or a tactical element like a tank section.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Headquarters">
  <data key="d0">Headquarters</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A command element within a company, battalion, or brigade.&lt;SEP&gt;An element of the Special Operations Joint Task Force that provides command and control of all forces in the task force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65ca07053c85879007a4b12d71977eb3</data>
