<node id="Army">
  <data key="d0">Army</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Army is the military service to which the described units and organizations belong, operating as a military organization with echelons ranging from fire teams to corps. As a military branch, it retains two tactical regiments and organizes division headquarters staff. In 2008, The Army established six warfighting functions that linked to joint functions. The Army serves as the military branch context for sustainment brigades and special operations forces, notably containing the largest number of special operations units within the Department of Defense. It functions as a higher-echelon service under whose operational control special operations task forces may operate.

Regarding specific capabilities, The Army contains the 95th Civil Affairs Brigade and utilizes Civil Affairs capabilities for missions. It also utilizes Psychological Operations units and special operations regiments for various military missions. For planning and modeling purposes, The Army uses rules of allocation to model force composition and employs special operations forces in wargaming scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b7fae9e6c5c9adcf919f15d77e75c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-272b00f6d97de5a3de8f78e2d6a7851e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2883359c75bc6fc3da995f38d6437f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46540f7346ac66e8acd8448d556926d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a07dcb1b08c46f988ffe232de0ba6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ba37bc0e16b243f02ab5b7be2e100c</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
