<node id="Surveillance">
  <data key="d0">Surveillance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A systematic, continuous collection of information involving active and passive activities that produces combat information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence Process">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A model consisting of four steps and two continuing activities that describes how the intelligence warfighting function facilitates situational understanding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Operations">
  <data key="d0">Security Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Operations performed by commanders to provide early warning of enemy operations and time for forces to react.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations performed by commanders to provide early warning of enemy operations, time and maneuver space for reaction, and protection for forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516fa4bb2c82a8017519f0c1ee450177</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Common Operational Picture">
  <data key="d0">Common Operational Picture</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A current and accurate representation of the area of operations shared with higher echelon, adjacent, subordinate, and tenant units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ADP 3-90">
  <data key="d0">ADP 3-90</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A publication titled Common Tactical Concepts and Echelons published on 31 July 2019.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-90 is an Army Doctrine Publication dated 31 July 2019, discussing common tactical concepts and echelons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-272b00f6d97de5a3de8f78e2d6a7851e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence Operations">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Tasks undertaken by military intelligence units through intelligence disciplines to obtain information to satisfy validated requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence Disciplines">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence Disciplines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific fields of intelligence collection, including counterintelligence, geospatial intelligence, and human intelligence, among others.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Information">
  <data key="d0">Combat Information</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Information produced by surveillance and reconnaissance that meets one or more of the commander’s critical information requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commander's Critical Information Requirements">
  <data key="d0">Commander's Critical Information Requirements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical information requirements that combat information is intended to meet or satisfy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Higher Echelon Headquarters">
  <data key="d0">Higher Echelon Headquarters</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A headquarters that imposes control measures within a subordinate unit's area of operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy">
  <data key="d0">Enemy</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The opposing force or threat whose operations, actions, and terrain are the focus of reconnaissance and security measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The opposing force or threat against which security operations provide early and accurate warning.&lt;SEP&gt;The opposing force or adversary against which friendly forces employ maneuver, fires, and defeat mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;The opposing force relative to friendly units, used as a reference for tactical mobility and supporting distance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a7610865bc56fc73c1989a23548f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-272b00f6d97de5a3de8f78e2d6a7851e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516fa4bb2c82a8017519f0c1ee450177</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uncommitted Forces">
  <data key="d0">Uncommitted Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Forces not in contact with an enemy or deployed on a specific mission, used to exploit success or avoid failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces used by commanders to exploit success or avoid failure, exemplified by echelon reserves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Echelon Reserves">
  <data key="d0">Echelon Reserves</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific type of uncommitted force held back from the main effort to be used when needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decisive Operation">
  <data key="d0">Decisive Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Decisive Operation is the primary effort where maximum possible combat power is allocated through economy of force.&lt;SEP&gt;The operation that directly accomplishes the mission.&lt;SEP&gt;The main operation that receives the maximum possible combat power generated by economy of force measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The operation that directly accomplishes the mission and is the focus of the commander's efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8cfc7a602ac472213d15ef41cf6d81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-770e75b09bf3306fb7e43a79786bc058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43827b67edd15288722ea2a5a3a94f03</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forms of Maneuver">
  <data key="d0">Forms of Maneuver</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactical concepts covered in the chapter, related to offensive operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Distinct tactical combinations of fire and movement, including envelopment, frontal assault, infiltration, penetration, and turning movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dfd7a87dfd28f5856896abb13b5c87</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Envelopment">
  <data key="d0">Envelopment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of maneuver where forces bypass the enemy's front to strike at their flanks or rear.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frontal Assault">
  <data key="d0">Frontal Assault</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of maneuver where forces attack along the enemy's front.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Penetration">
  <data key="d0">Penetration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of maneuver used to break through enemy lines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Turning Movement">
  <data key="d0">Turning Movement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of maneuver designed to force the enemy to abandon their position.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forms of Defense">
  <data key="d0">Forms of Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactical concepts covered in the chapter, related to defensive operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Defensive arrangements including perimeter defense, defense of a linear obstacle, and reverse slope defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63dfd7a87dfd28f5856896abb13b5c87</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perimeter Defense">
  <data key="d0">Perimeter Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of defense oriented in all directions to protect a specific location.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defense of a Linear Obstacle">
  <data key="d0">Defense of a Linear Obstacle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of defense conducted along a specific terrain feature or boundary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reverse Slope Defense">
  <data key="d0">Reverse Slope Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of defense conducted on the slope of a hill or ridge that is hidden from enemy observation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Task Organization">
  <data key="d0">Task Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of organizing available capabilities to accomplish the mission and generate combined arms effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marine Corps">
  <data key="d0">Marine Corps</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military organization that utilizes the section unit structure alongside the Army.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crew">
  <data key="d0">Crew</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A small military unit consisting of all personnel operating a particular system, such as a mortar or tank.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778744565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Division">
  <data key="d0">Division</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit responsible for controlling assigned airspace and integrating airspace use between brigades.&lt;SEP&gt;An Army echelon higher than a brigade and part of a corps.&lt;SEP&gt;An echelon of command and tactical formation that employs brigade combat teams and brigades to achieve objectives on land.&lt;SEP&gt;A Division receives complementary effects supporting freedom of action from special operations joint task forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b023ae1c5d93443720b726ec81502bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a7d3d9560fe2b56cedf3cfdaba2f4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc098f3a3543d54bc8f0881ae2eae85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12f6aa4929841ed6a30ffdcdab213e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67</data>
