<node id="1st Special Forces Command">
  <data key="d0">1st Special Forces Command</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Mans, trains, equips, validates, and deploys Army special operations forces globally; serves as Army core of deployable special operations joint task force headquarters.&lt;SEP&gt;A command assigning two Active Component Psychological Operations groups.&lt;SEP&gt;A two-star headquarters that organizes and deploys as the core of a special operations joint task force headquarters.&lt;SEP&gt;The 95th Civil Affairs Brigade is assigned to support commanders within this command.&lt;SEP&gt;The higher command to which the 528th Sustainment Brigade is subordinate and receives essential support from the brigade.&lt;SEP&gt;A command supported by the 528th Sustainment Brigade, 112th Signal Battalion, and 389th Military Intelligence Battalion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2883359c75bc6fc3da995f38d6437f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1118e47016e1aacd6394fca251ed2dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a83d27ea86b67140cb6a36139ae1786c</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="USASOC">
  <data key="d0">USASOC</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Directs 1st Special Forces Command to fulfill theater combatant command and joint staff validated missions.&lt;SEP&gt;United States Army Special Operations Command, for which the 528th Sustainment Brigade serves as the lead component for logistics.&lt;SEP&gt;The organization to which the 528th Sustainment Brigade is assigned and responsible for SOF-peculiar sustainment requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;USASOC is the command for which Psychological Operations units lead influence efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2883359c75bc6fc3da995f38d6437f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Forces Groups">
  <data key="d0">Special Forces Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Consist of one headquarters and headquarters company, one group support battalion, and four Special Forces battalions; five active-duty and two National Guard groups assigned to 1st Special Forces Command.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Forces Battalion">
  <data key="d0">Special Forces Battalion</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Forms nucleus of special operations task force; consists of headquarters, support companies, and three Special Forces companies.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit whose commander and staff normally establish a special operations task force.&lt;SEP&gt;A Special Forces battalion is a unit level that should be aligned with conventional force divisions or corps-level joint task forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Forces Operational Detachment-Bravo">
  <data key="d0">Special Forces Operational Detachment-Bravo</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Command and control element; exercises command of up to six Special Forces operational detachments–alpha; establishes advanced operations bases or isolation facilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Forces Operational Detachment-Alpha">
  <data key="d0">Special Forces Operational Detachment-Alpha</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary Special Forces operational unit; has language and cultural expertise; static-line airborne qualified; six per company.&lt;SEP&gt;A Special Forces operational detachment-alpha is a unit that can generate or operate with 300 to 500 personnel when working with resistance forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Guard">
  <data key="d0">National Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Contributes two Special Forces groups assigned to 1st Special Forces Command.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Theater Combatant Command">
  <data key="d0">Theater Combatant Command</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Receives support from 1st Special Forces Command units to meet operational requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Staff">
  <data key="d0">Joint Staff</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Validates missions for 1st Special Forces Command in support of global campaign plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advanced Operations Base">
  <data key="d0">Advanced Operations Base</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Small, light, tailored element established by Operational Detachment–Bravo for specific missions like forward launch and recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;A small, temporary base established near or within a joint operations area to command and support special operations.&lt;SEP&gt;An advanced operations base is a facility such as an airfield, pier, or anchorage that is normally fixed but may displace during armed conflict to ensure survivability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec1050b8c05b4ecb8bdb51a5d2c0abb</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isolation Facilities">
  <data key="d0">Isolation Facilities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Facilities facilitated by special operations task force for isolation and preparation of operational detachments–alpha.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Operations Command And Control Element">
  <data key="d0">Special Operations Command And Control Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Facilitates command relationships between joint special operations task force and battalion headquarters.&lt;SEP&gt;An element task organized for integration into corps or higher-echelon operations to synchronize special and conventional operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b01db05e3701dde254ad8d25610798</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Group Support Battalion">
  <data key="d0">Group Support Battalion</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific unit component within Special Forces Groups providing support functions.&lt;SEP&gt;A group support battalion is included within a Special Forces group to meet unique sustainment needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Headquarters and Headquarters Detachment">
  <data key="d0">Headquarters and Headquarters Detachment</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific unit component within Special Forces Battalions responsible for command and control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battalion Support Company">
  <data key="d0">Battalion Support Company</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific unit component within Special Forces Battalions providing support functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forward Support Company">
  <data key="d0">Forward Support Company</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific unit component within Special Forces Battalions providing forward support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United States Army">
  <data key="d0">United States Army</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The military branch that USASOC serves as a component for and designates the JFK Special Warfare Center as a Center of Excellence.&lt;SEP&gt;The parent organization possessing four Psychological Operations groups.&lt;SEP&gt;The broader military organization to which Special Forces Groups belong.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1118e47016e1aacd6394fca251ed2dba</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 3-05">
  <data key="d0">JP 3-05</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A Joint Publication referenced in the text regarding special operations capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;JP 3-05 is a joint publication referenced regarding the definition of a special operations joint task force.&lt;SEP&gt;JP 3-05 is a joint publication cited regarding the definition of Theater Special Operations Command.&lt;SEP&gt;A publication referenced regarding the definition of joint special operations task force.&lt;SEP&gt;A joint publication referenced regarding special operations command and control elements.&lt;SEP&gt;A joint publication referenced in the definition of the Joint Special Operations Task Force.&lt;SEP&gt;JP 3-05 is a publication referenced for information on liaison officers and joint special operations air components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2c950368aaaddb9954e21827ca6fc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65ca07053c85879007a4b12d71977eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b01db05e3701dde254ad8d25610798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec1050b8c05b4ecb8bdb51a5d2c0abb</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unconventional Warfare">
  <data key="d0">Unconventional Warfare</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A key capability emphasis for Special Forces Groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Unconventional warfare is a core activity executed by Special Forces Soldiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Operations Joint Task Force">
  <data key="d0">Special Operations Joint Task Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployable joint task force structure for which 1st Special Forces Command serves as the Army core.&lt;SEP&gt;A joint task force supported by the 528th Sustainment Brigade's logistics synchronization capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;A Special Operations Joint Task Force is an organization from two or more Military Departments organized to provide command and control of joint special operations forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Task Force">
  <data key="d0">Joint Task Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A command structure under which Special Forces Groups may operate when deployed.&lt;SEP&gt;A Joint Task Force is a joint force constituted and designated to accomplish a specific mission.&lt;SEP&gt;A joint force that is enabled by the Special Operations Joint Task Force with intelligence and targeting capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65ca07053c85879007a4b12d71977eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Training Events">
  <data key="d0">Training Events</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Exercises and training activities conducted by units within 1st Special Forces Command to enable integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="528th Sustainment Brigade">
  <data key="d0">528th Sustainment Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A unique Army sustainment brigade maintaining global situational awareness of deployed Army special operations forces' logistics support.&lt;SEP&gt;A subordinate unit of 1st Special Forces Command responsible for setting operational logistic conditions and providing support to special operations worldwide.&lt;SEP&gt;The 528th Sustainment Brigade is a unique Army sustainment brigade maintaining global situational awareness of deployed Army special operations forces' logistics support structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2883359c75bc6fc3da995f38d6437f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a07dcb1b08c46f988ffe232de0ba6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support Operations Section">
  <data key="d0">Support Operations Section</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A key component of the 528th Sustainment Brigade that exercises directive authority over subordinate units and manages sustainment operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Army Service Component Command">
  <data key="d0">Army Service Component Command</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A command entity in the vicinity of which the 528th Sustainment Brigade Headquarters is typically located.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="112th Signal Battalion">
  <data key="d0">112th Signal Battalion</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A battalion trained, resourced, and equipped by the 528th Sustainment Brigade in support of special operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The 112th Signal Battalion is the Army's only special operations signal battalion, trained and equipped by the 528th Sustainment Brigade.&lt;SEP&gt;The 112th Signal Battalion deployed communications assemblage teams to support Special Operations Command–South headquarters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2883359c75bc6fc3da995f38d6437f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2c950368aaaddb9954e21827ca6fc1</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="389th Military Intelligence Battalion">
  <data key="d0">389th Military Intelligence Battalion</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A battalion trained, resourced, and equipped by the 528th Sustainment Brigade in support of special operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A subordinate unit of the 528th Sustainment Brigade providing timely and accurate intelligence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2883359c75bc6fc3da995f38d6437f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United States Army Special Operations Aviation Command">
  <data key="d0">United States Army Special Operations Aviation Command</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the three key subordinate commands around which USASOC is organized.&lt;SEP&gt;Oversees functions including training, doctrine, and operations for Army special operations aviation and provides command oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States Army Special Operations Aviation Command is the organization depicted in Figure 1-7 overseeing special operations aviation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1118e47016e1aacd6394fca251ed2dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-634019196f631f7ab3b7db7cf3971a9d</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Operations">
  <data key="d0">Special Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Activities conducted by USASOC and 1st Special Forces Command across the full range of military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Military activities conducted by special operations forces requiring specific logistics, medical, and aviation support to enable mission success.&lt;SEP&gt;Military operations involving air, land, and maritime assets that require synchronization with conventional operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1118e47016e1aacd6394fca251ed2dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b01db05e3701dde254ad8d25610798</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Logistics Support">
  <data key="d0">Logistics Support</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Essential support provided by the 528th Sustainment Brigade to enable special operations missions and set operational conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Role II Medical Support">
  <data key="d0">Role II Medical Support</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical holding capabilities provided by the 528th Sustainment Brigade to deployed Army special operations forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Essential support provided by the 528th Sustainment Brigade to the 1st Special Forces Command.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2883359c75bc6fc3da995f38d6437f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unmanned Aerial Vehicles">
  <data key="d0">Unmanned Aerial Vehicles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SOF-specific aircraft provided by the 160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment for precision aviation support and unmanned aircraft system support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Force Special Operations Component Commander">
  <data key="d0">Joint Force Special Operations Component Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The commander provided with aviation capabilities by the 160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment to conduct fires and intelligence operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755276</data>
