</node>
<node id="Combatant Commander">
  <data key="d0">Combatant Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A role receiving adaptable forces and campaign plans from Special Forces and Psychological Operations groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Senior military leader whose objectives and campaign plans are supported by Psychological Operations units.&lt;SEP&gt;The Combatant Commander receives principal special operations advice from the theater special operations commander.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2c950368aaaddb9954e21827ca6fc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a83d27ea86b67140cb6a36139ae1786c</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Force Commander">
  <data key="d0">Joint Force Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A role receiving support and influence fires from Psychological Operations groups.&lt;SEP&gt;A commander supported by Civil Affairs capabilities for missions and areas of operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Joint Force Commander develops campaign plans supported by special operations aviation units and the 75th Ranger Regiment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Joint Force Commander assigns joint special operations areas and establishes command relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual who uses the joint special operations task force to plan and conduct special operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A joint force commander is supported by Psychological Operations units during combat operations and information activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-634019196f631f7ab3b7db7cf3971a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a07dcb1b08c46f988ffe232de0ba6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partner Forces">
  <data key="d0">Partner Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Forces worked with and through by Special Forces Operational Detachment–Alpha.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conventional Forces">
  <data key="d0">Conventional Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Forces distinct from Special Forces, which Special Forces do not replace or substitute.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces compared to Civil Affairs teams regarding freedom of movement in competition.&lt;SEP&gt;Conventional Forces are military units that integrate and interoperate with special operations forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Military forces that coordinate with special operations through liaison elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Conventional Forces may have selected special operations aviation assets placed under their control by SOF commanders.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces that may augment joint SOF staff to sustain capability for more than six months or be included in task force augmentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Conventional forces are military units that special operations forces liaison elements may be embedded with or operate alongside.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b01db05e3701dde254ad8d25610798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a07dcb1b08c46f988ffe232de0ba6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec1050b8c05b4ecb8bdb51a5d2c0abb</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specialized Skills">
  <data key="d0">Specialized Skills</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Capabilities including intelligence, sniper techniques, demolitions, and medical training possessed by operational detachments–alpha.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Influence Activities">
  <data key="d0">Influence Activities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operations planned and executed by Psychological Operations groups in the information environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Primary function of Psychological Operations units to create and reinforce desired behaviors in selected individuals and groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a83d27ea86b67140cb6a36139ae1786c</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
