<node id="Command And Control">
  <data key="d0">Command And Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Command And Control is critical to the success of military operations and enables commanders to make informed decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Command And Control is required for effective management of Psychological Operations and Civil Affairs units.&lt;SEP&gt;Command And Control is a function provided by the Regimental Headquarters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e2c950368aaaddb9954e21827ca6fc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ba37bc0e16b243f02ab5b7be2e100c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eaac3759faff54df152d27018118936</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AC-130 Gunship">
  <data key="d0">AC-130 Gunship</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The AC-130 Gunship provided fire support to the 7th Special Forces Group element.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e2c950368aaaddb9954e21827ca6fc1</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Theater Special Operations Command">
  <data key="d0">Theater Special Operations Command</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Theater Special Operations Command facilitates regional partnerships and ensures operational access for mission success.&lt;SEP&gt;The Theater Special Operations Command is a subordinate unified command established by United States Special Operations Command under a combatant commander.&lt;SEP&gt;Serves as a command and control bridge during escalation from crisis to conflict, preceding the establishment of a Special Operations Joint Task Force headquarters.&lt;SEP&gt;A command that may deploy a special operations command–forward and establish various task forces.&lt;SEP&gt;A Theater Special Operations Command is an operational command under which a joint special operations air component may fall.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e2c950368aaaddb9954e21827ca6fc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65ca07053c85879007a4b12d71977eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec1050b8c05b4ecb8bdb51a5d2c0abb</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 1, Volume 2">
  <data key="d0">JP 1, Volume 2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">JP 1, Volume 2 is a joint publication cited regarding the definition of command and control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e2c950368aaaddb9954e21827ca6fc1</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
