<node id="Special Operations Task Force">
  <data key="d0">Special Operations Task Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A task force typically supported by a Civil Affairs company during deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;A scalable unit, normally of battalion size, providing command and control for special operations activities.&lt;SEP&gt;A commander entity that may elect to employ special operations command and control elements.&lt;SEP&gt;A Special Operations Task Force controls and supports an advanced operations base at a main or forward operations base.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b01db05e3701dde254ad8d25610798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a07dcb1b08c46f988ffe232de0ba6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec1050b8c05b4ecb8bdb51a5d2c0abb</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Forces Group Headquarters">
  <data key="d0">Special Forces Group Headquarters</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
