<node id="Joint Special Operations Task Force">
  <data key="d0">Joint Special Operations Task Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Joint Special Operations Task Force is a task force formed to conduct special operations, composed of special operations forces from one or more Services or personnel from other United States Government departments and agencies. In certain contexts, it is established by Special Forces groups when augmented by other services, and potentially combines with United States Government departments or multinational SOF. The primary purpose of a Joint Special Operations Task Force is to control SOF assets and integrate special operations requirements.

The command and control architecture of the entity can be supplemented by special operations detachments. It may employ special operations command and control elements and provides liaison elements to facilitate operations. Functionally, the task force provides assets to augment an advanced operations base for specific mission sets. Within this operational framework, the 75th Ranger Regiment operates as a rapid response force subordinate to a Joint Special Operations Task Force, demonstrating the hierarchy and capability integration inherent to the organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65ca07053c85879007a4b12d71977eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c96559ad2979a6465236d374730b783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b01db05e3701dde254ad8d25610798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ba37bc0e16b243f02ab5b7be2e100c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec1050b8c05b4ecb8bdb51a5d2c0abb</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778755321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FM 3-05">
  <data key="d0">FM 3-05</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">FM 3-05 is an Army Field Manual dated 26 June 2025 that serves as a comprehensive doctrinal document for Army Special Operations Forces. The manual outlines the organization, capabilities, and employment considerations of these forces, including specific information on regiment operations and the structure of special operations detachments within USASOC. Chapter 1 of the document addresses Army Special Operations Forces characteristics, while other sections detail the Command and Control structure essential for special operations forces.

The content extends to specific functional areas and units, providing information on Psychological Operations and the Civil Affairs brigade structure, capabilities, and employment considerations. Sustainment is also covered, with specific references to the 528th Sustainment Brigade and Army Special Operations Forces sustainment logistics. Additionally, FM 3-05 includes doctrine for Rangers and defines the roles of coordinating elements and liaison officers within the operational framework. This publication consolidates critical information regarding the command, control, and support structures necessary for effective special operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d083ee11e02b24e5e46d8ecfba9df6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27d7d56a1c67174500dfb742aa9fc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51979d8934c76925b7391cb149c853a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2883359c75bc6fc3da995f38d6437f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1118e47016e1aacd6394fca251ed2dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2c950368aaaddb9954e21827ca6fc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65ca07053c85879007a4b12d71977eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c2c3d76fec30a58c9326c2f2fbff67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-634019196f631f7ab3b7db7cf3971a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c96559ad2979a6465236d374730b783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f24a47cacf5b4d8c879d2cac52eda18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46540f7346ac66e8acd8448d556926d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b01db05e3701dde254ad8d25610798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7124d28a5494b25065ecde8dbfca305b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a07dcb1b08c46f988ffe232de0ba6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ba37bc0e16b243f02ab5b7be2e100c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec1050b8c05b4ecb8bdb51a5d2c0abb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a83d27ea86b67140cb6a36139ae1786c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eaac3759faff54df152d27018118936</data>
